This disc contains BigLander, an extended version
of Lander that has a larger landscape and
keyboard support.

The Arthur directory contains BigLander for
Arthur.

The RISC_OS directory contains BigLander for all
versions of RISC OS.

BigLander comes in four landscape sizes, each of
which is in a folder giving the landscape size:

* 13x11 tile corners (suitable for ARM2)

* 20x20 tile corners (suitable for ARM3)

* 65x65 tile corners (suitable for StrongARM)

* 122x122 tile corners (suitable for Raspberry Pi)

To get the number of tiles in each direction,
subtract 1 from the number of tile corners, so
the first option contains 12x10 tiles, just like
the original Lander.

Choose the relevant folder for your system. You
can run all versions on all systems, but large
landscapes will run more slowly.

More information can be found by clicking Menu on
!BigLander and choosing Help.

See lander.bbcelite.com/hacks for details.